MID_LIB_Hub_Memory001_t: Mediators I
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory001_m01_001: It is anticipated that a variety of problems may\noccur during the generational voyages the\nSerpent-Series ships embark upon. From structural\ndamage, to civil unrest among the crew, to contact\nwith unknown intelligent lifeforms, it is impossible\nto plan for every situation that may arise.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory001_m01_002: Enter Mediators, artificial humans produced within\nthe Serpents as problem solvers. Their main role is\nto facilitate conflict resolution among parties\ninvolved in a dispute. As such, they may be called on\nto respond in a variety of ways, addressing these\nissues with dialogue or with force as necessary.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory002_t: Mediators II
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory002_m01_001: Mediators are sampled from the genetic code of over\neight million specimens. Their appearance is\nstatistically favorable, their bones and muscles are\nengineered to be denser than normal, and higher-\ndimension quantum reactors allow their lifespans\nto endure the long voyage of a Serpent-Series ship.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory002_m01_002: Furthermore, in anticipation of the possibility that a\nMediator is the sole survivor of unforeseen extreme\ncircumstances, they are designed to be capable of\na variety of methods of reproduction to ensure the\nsurvival of human civilization. This is an important\nphysical feature of all Mediators.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory002_m01_003: The numerous enhancements made to the bodies of\nMediators are intended to be maintained by the\nValen particles produced as a byproduct of their\nhigher-dimension quantum reactors. Any flaws\nin this system could lead to serious problems,\nincluding rapid aging of the body.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory003_t: Mediators III
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory003_m01_001: If a Mediator is produced, it is likely in response to\ntrouble on a Serpent-Series ship. In order to improve\nthe chances of resolution, multiple models are\navailable for different purposes. Here are a few\nexamples of Mediator models and their specialties.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory003_m01_002: Ulysses\nThe most basic model. Their appearance is\nunremarkable, making it hard to tell them apart from\nnormal humans. Though they lack the specialized\nabilities found in other models, they are skilled at\ninfiltrating organizations.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory003_m01_003: Ikaros\nThis model is designed for very low atmospheric\npressure, and is able to function in inhospitable\nenvironments such as underwater. It has high\npotential for improvement. It is marked by a feather-\nlike organ on the head that absorbs ambient aether.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory003_m01_004: Gyges\nIts particularly large physique lets it excel in strength\nneeded for work on civil-engineering projects. In\nexchange, they are less nimble than others. Since this\nrole is often filled by Titanus, we anticipate fewer\nuse cases for this model of Mediator.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory003_m01_005: Arion\nA model intended for direct physical combat. They\nexcel in strength, agility, and endurance. This model\nis distinguished by its hair resembling a burning\nmane, which serves to convert the heat generated in\ntheir bodies into light as it efficiently dissipates.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory004_t: Heart Cores I
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory004_m01_001: Officially called Heart Core Reactors, they are also\nknown as higher-dimension quantum reactors.\nThese semi-perpetual motion machines were put into\npractical use after several revolutionary innovations\nonce thought impossible. They are truly the\ncrystallization of human ingenuity.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory004_m01_002: A hyperspace is formed inside the Heart Core\nReactor, and mass is injected into the sealed\nsingularity from the outside, radiating heat as the\nprimary product. It is possible to efficiently extract\nValen particles through a quasi-Calabi-Yau manifold\ntransformation in response.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory004_m01_003: A human implanted with one can enjoy a lifespan\nfar beyond normal bounds as a side effect of the\nValen particles generated. However, the true\nbenefit of the Heart Core Reactor is its allowance\nfor using an unlimited quantity of Valen particles.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory004_m01_004: Because creating a Heart Core Reactor requires\nengineering technology and an extremely high level\nof manufacturing precision, it may be impossible\nto produce new ones in the post-Great Undoing\nworld. We estimate that there are one hundred\nor fewer units still functioning on the surface.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory005_t: Heart Cores II
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory005_m01_001: Because the technologies used to manufacture Heart\nCore Reactors vary greatly, as do their individual\ncharacteristics, it is relatively easy to classify them\ninto generations.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory005_m01_002: Prototypes\nThe earliest model, used to prove the foundational\ntheory of higher-dimension quantum reactors,\nwas the size of a city. After many iterations, the\npreproduction prototype model was successfully\nminiaturized to the size of a railcar.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory005_m01_003: Generation 1\nThese models, which were substantially smaller than\nprevious versions, entered stable mass production.\nThe improved Gen-1.5 models were miniaturized\nfurther, finally allowing for installation in humans.\nThis began a new stage of research into them.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory005_m01_004: Generation 2\nThis model had dramatically improved functionality.\nMaximum output was greatly increased, and lifespan\nextension increased by orders of magnitude. Many of\nthe crew on board Serpent-Series ships had this\nmodel installed.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory005_m01_005: Generation 3\nA material called epimenium, synthesized from a\nrevolutionary new element, allowed for this model to\nhave higher mental synchronicity. Early versions\nwere somewhat error-prone, but later improvements\nresulted in a high level of stable function.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory006_t: Epimenium
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory006_m01_001: A powdered alloy created by processing a new\nelement discovered by the scientist Epimenides.\nIts greatest trait is its ability to resonate with human\nbrain waves. Named for its discoverer, epimenium\nremains one of the landmark accomplishments\nof aether physics.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory006_m01_002: It is unknown just what spurred Epimenides to\ndevise this revolutionary material. One theory,\nstill speculative, suggests that Epimenides was\nresearching ways to preserve all his knowledge\neternally, and that this substance was merely one\nfruit of those efforts.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory006_m01_003: There are also records of intriguing speculation\nsubmitted by the Oracle Katarina, who suggests that\nepimenium may have been a result of Epimenides\nsearching for a means to preserve his soul externally\nin some way.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory007_t: Grand Megaliths
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory007_m01_001: The collective name given to computer devices that\nmeet either the Grand Megalith-class quantum\ncomputing standard or one of similar scope. Each\nappears as a single slab with a silicon exterior.\nThe name originates from their likeness to the stone\nstructures often seen in ancient civilizations.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory007_m01_002: The Grand Megaliths are placed in all Districts\nacross the world, spaced regularly to distribute the\nburden of communications and advanced information\nprocessing. Every Megalith is positioned in a\nparallel hierarchy, save for Vritra, who ranks above\nthem all.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory008_t: Subsurface Zones
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory008_m01_001: The large-scale underground structures built all over\nthe world have different purposes depending on\nwhen and where they were built. Each has a unique\nEX number assigned by the Alliance of the Great\nAcolytes of Recondite Technology and Harmonic\nAlignment. A selection are described here.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory008_m01_002: EX-017\nAn anti-strategic-arms shelter built in the eastern\nregion of the former District 1. It is big enough to be\ncalled an underground city and is managed by the\nGrand Megalith Fermi. Its status is unknown due to\nKunlun's sudden disconnection from the network.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory008_m01_003: EX-053\nAn experimentation facility that doubles as an\nemergency shelter. It avoided severe damage during\nthe Great Undoing. It has a gigantic reservoir for\nobservation experiments, and is managed by the\nGrand Megalith Ptolemaios.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory008_m01_004: EX-061\nOriginally built as a strategic military base, it is also\nequipped with a dry dock for building Serpent-Series\nships. It is large even among EX-series subsurface\nzones—so immense, in fact, that it spans the desert.\nIt is managed by the Grand Megalith Magellan.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory008_m01_005: EX-089\nAn experimentation facility equipped with a gigantic\nparticle accelerator. It is managed by the Grand\nMegalith Hannibal. Within it is the sealed facility\nEX-189, which was once used for weapons testing\nbut was closed due to loss of systems control.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory008_m01_006: EX-502\nThis subsurface zone serves as the base of an orbital\nlift device used to transport supplies into satellite\norbit. It is managed by the Grand Megalith Lancelot.\nIts status is unknown due to Kunlun's sudden\ndisconnection from the network.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory009_t: Kunlun
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory009_m01_001: Kunlun is the name for the autonomous network\ncomprised of the Grand Megaliths of former District\n7 that escaped damage in the Great Undoing and\ncontinue to operate, as well as Chang'e, the brain of\nSerpent-Series Craft 18, Nuwa. It is also the\ncollective name for the operators of that network.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory009_m01_002: Kunlun is a closed network cut off from Vritra. While\nit maintains perfect autonomy, this naturally comes\nat the cost of the ability to share information with\nthe wider communications network. For that reason,\nKunlun's records have scarcely been updated since\nthe Great Undoing.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory010_t: Vritra I
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory010_m01_001: Vritra is undoubtedly the largest artificial intelligence\nin human history. Even before the Great Undoing, it\nwas ranked above all of the Grand Megaliths across\nthe world. It presides over their network so that it\ncan collate and process their information.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory010_m01_002: The main body of Vritra was constructed on the far\nside of the moon, and is currently not visible from\nthe surface. Considering Vritra's powerful self-repair\ncapabilities, it is believed to be self-propagating,\nenlarging itself, and greatly expanding its functions.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory010_m01_003: One assumes that, like the other Grand Megaliths,\nVritra has an artificial personality to interface with.\nHowever, details on this are extremely confidential\nand could not be ascertained. Information on it is so\nfragmentary that it would be difficult even to guess\nat what it might be.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory010_m01_004: It is unclear what Vritra, who is still active, might be\nplanning. The fact remains that, since Kunlun's\nnetwork is cut off from communication with Vritra,\nwe have no window into its machinations. Further\nspeculation would be pointless based on so little\nhard data.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory011_t: Vritra II
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory011_m01_001: The idea of using surgical means to install a Heart\nCore in a human body to augment it originated with\nVritra. Investigations up to this point have revealed\nthat, curiously, the resulting structure is similar to the\nphysical structure of those who descend from the\nalien entity that calls itself a god.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory011_m01_002: But what if this similarity is not coincidental, but\nthe result of clear intent? The Grand Megalith\nCassiopeia theorizes that Vritra may have been in\nsome form of contact with the alien entity since\nbefore the Great Undoing. However, we lack the\nevidence to prove this.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory012_t: Agartha I
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory012_m01_001: Before the Great Undoing, numerous technologies\nthat defied conventional wisdom were created by\na supranational group known as the Alliance of the\nGreat Acolytes of Recondite Technology and\nHarmonic Alignment. They more commonly went\nby the acronym AGARTHA.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory012_m01_002: It is still unclear what links Agartha, the organization\nthat Anacharsis named when he spoke to the\nGrand Megalith Katarina, with the original\nAGARTHA, but there is currently no doubt that\nthey serve Vritra.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory012_m01_003: Furthermore, querying past records for the name\nAnacharsis revealed a record of a person with the\nsame name in what was District 1 prior to the Great\nUndoing. It should be noted that he was a researcher\nspecializing in biochemistry.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory013_t: Agartha II
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory013_m01_001: AGARTHA was a supranational group founded on\nthe ideal of overcoming national borders to conduct\njoint research into new technologies. Collaboration\nbetween the idealistic and passionate researchers\nwho participated due to ideological sympathies\nbrought about revolutionary technologies.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory013_m01_002: Their historic achievements include Titanus tech\nbased on micromachines, advanced gravity control,\nsuperluminal communications, spatial transfer\ntechnology, novel semiperpetual-motion machines,\nthe aether physics that paved the way for all of these,\nand the birth of new human beings adapted to space.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory014_t: Titanus
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory014_m01_001: Titanus is the term for a moving structure made of\nmicromachines and the silicon abundant in soil.\nThey can be created whenever and wherever they\nare required, so long as there is sand present.\nThis revolutionary technology upended the very\nfoundation of the concept of machines.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory014_m01_002: A capacitor serves as their structural core, around\nwhich micromachines synthesize a silicon-based\napparatus. They can operate until they run out\nof stored power, at which point they lose structural\nintegrity and break down, returning to sand.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory014_m01_003: Although they appear to act autonomously, they do\nnot actually have self-determination. All of their\ndecisions and controls are handled by local Grand\nMegaliths. For that reason, the use of Titanus is\nlimited in regions outside of their reach.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory015_t: Salamanders
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory015_m01_001: Salamanders are portable firearms once\nmanufactured for and issued to Nuwa's crew.\nOfficially known as Electric Cannon 96C, they\nexpend the electricity stored in the capacitor at\ntheir tip to fire charged particle beams, making\nfor effective long-range attacks.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory015_m01_002: Because Salamanders are small and easy to handle\nand operate, even those with no magical training can\nuse them. For this reason, there is a risk of accidents\nif they are used carelessly, and it is necessary to\nhandle them with abundant caution.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory016_t: Zerberus
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory016_m01_001: The Electric Cannon 96C Mk. II, commonly known\nas Zerberus, is an upgraded model of the Salamander\nmade specifically for the Mediator Troy. While\nextremely powerful, its balance is poor, making it\ndifficult to use without a Mediator's augmented\nmusculature.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory016_m01_002: It is an unusual-looking weapon that hardly\nresembles the original thanks to two additional\nmuzzles and capacitors, installed to support the\nmaximum possible output. It also has severe issues\nwith portability and concealment due to its excessive\nincrease in size.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory017_t: Artemis
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory017_m01_001: Artemis is the series name for ground surveillance\nsatellites launched in the past. A total of 16 were\nlaunched to observe the surface from geosynchronous\norbit. Kunlun has succeeded in taking control of the\none positioned above District 7.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory017_m01_002: All Artemis units can fire superheavy metal\nprojectiles from orbit, which hold enormous\ndestructive power due to gravitational acceleration.\nThis was used against the hostile life-form that\nemerged during the Great Undoing, proving the\neffectiveness of physical attacks against the target.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory017_m01_003: The lenses of artificial sapphire installed in Artemis\nwere expected to be usable for a thousand years or\nlonger, but their utility was greatly decreased by the\naccumulation of dust thrown up from the surface\nduring the Great Undoing. They have now lost the\nmajority of their capacity to observe the surface.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory017_m01_004: After the Great Undoing, one crew member made the\nfollowing sardonic remark: "We designed Artemis's\neyes to last thousands of years, but we somehow\nforgot to give her eyelids. A few seconds' thought\nshould have been enough to realize that cataract\nremoval in space would be tricky."
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory018_t: Project Ouroboros
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory018_m01_001: After being drafted by Vritra, this project was\napproved by AGARTHA and put into action as a\ngreat work of human cooperation. Its purpose was\nto build multiple interstellar ships and send them to\nobserve unknown environments, investigate\nhabitable planets, and settle the cosmos.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory018_m01_002: Common features of these interstellar ships included\nhulls with self-repair and self-expansion functions\nbased in Titanus technology, high-performance\nconversion reactors capable of using mass as a power\nsource, and quantum computing devices up to\nGrand Megalith standards.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory018_m01_003: Each ship was named for a serpent found in world\nmythology. This is the reason that the ships built\nfor Project Ouroboros are also called Serpents.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory019_t: Ouroboros-Class
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory019_m01_001: Ouroboros-class ships were produced in the early\nstages of the project. They have a huge cylindrical\nliving space in the hull, capable of hosting up to four\nmillion people. Artificial gravity inside is produced\nby rotation; due to this characteristic structure, the\nCoriolis effect is always active in the interior.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory019_m01_002: This scale was not intended at the outset of the\nproject. Due to design goals changing partway\nthrough, it is simply an enlarged version of Craft 0,\nOhmononushi, the Serpent-Series prototype. The\nheavy-handed design was long criticized for its lack\nof optimization for each part.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory019_m01_003: The hulls of Ouroboros-class ships were so large that\nthey could not be constructed on the ground. Work\nwas therefore carried out in space instead. Some\nparts were individually manufactured on the ground\nand launched into space for assembly.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory019_m01_004: The first of these ships was the flagship, Craft 1,\nOuroboros, and the last was Craft 13, Ryūō. After\nthis, development shifted to the next-generation\nEchidna-class ships for the latter part of the project,\nending construction on the Ouroboros-class.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory020_t: Echidna-Class
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory020_m01_001: Echidna-class ships were designed after deploying\nthe Ouroboros class, and feature solutions to many of\ntheir longstanding problems. They are significantly\nsmaller than Ouroboros-class ships, and replaced the\nconventional inertial gravity generators in the\nresidential sector with more cutting-edge methods.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory020_m01_002: It is noteworthy that, while normally Serpent\ncommunication must be relayed through Vritra, the\nEchidna-class is uniquely capable of using a special\ndedicated network to communicate with other\nvessels of its model without intermediary nodes.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory020_m01_003: The construction plans for Craft 14, Echidna,\nthrough Craft 20, Tiamat, were proposed by Vritra\nand approved by the Alliance. Capacity settled at\nabout 1.5 million people, about a third of the\nOuroboros class's four million. However, the dramatic\nsize reduction came with many benefits.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory020_m01_004: Because the Great Undoing occurred immediately\nafter the launch of Craft 18, Nuwa, construction\nplans for Craft 19, Quetzalcoatl, and Craft 20,\nTiamat, were suspended and then abandoned.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory021_t: Seven-Star Harmony
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory021_m01_001: The seven-star harmony is a secret technique\nunique to Kunlun that combines the ancient concept\nof energy flow with the principles of yoga.\nIt empowers the user's body by applying energy\nflow to the meridians and seven celestial wells\nthroughout the body, directing force inward.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory021_m01_002: The technique was devised by Roxana, who once\nserved as Nuwa's combat captain, as a method of\nexplosive effectiveness enhancement through linking\nthe whole body's meridians and celestial wells. It has\nbecome well-understood in Kunlun over the years.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory021_m01_003: When a human with a Heart Core, such as a ship's\ncrewman, masters this technique, they can make the\npower generated by their Heart Core surge through\nthe meridians, directing energy to their whole bodies.\nThis circulated and refined energy results in further\namplification and tremendous augmentation.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory021_m01_004: Simple augmentation using energy flow through\nmeridians without involving the celestial wells is\ncalled meridian rotation, and is distinct from the\nseven-star harmony technique. It is thought to calm\nthe mind and improve blood flow, and a number of\nvillagers in Kunlun have mastered it.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory022_t: Seven-Star Engine
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory022_m01_001: The seven-star engine is a special design given only\nto Mediator Anatolia. It consists of the Heart Core,\nlike a primary star, and six small capacitors, like\nlesser stars, placed at the seven celestial wells.\nIt is based on a theory once proposed by Roxana.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory022_m01_002: The purpose of the seven-star engine is to multiply\nthe power of the energy flowing through the body. It\ntakes years of training to fully control. It has been\ntheorized that if a bearer of the seven-star engine\ncould perfect the seven-star harmony, the door to a\nnew secret technique would open.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory023_t: Kunlun Magic
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory023_m01_001: A collective term for the unique magic developed by\nthose from Kunlun. Like spirit magic, it uses the\ncaster's own magic power and the aether in the\natmosphere, but it is unique in that it uses sand\nas its main material component in conjunction with\nmicromachines. A few examples are listed here.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory023_m01_002: Wandering Wall\nThe caster can instantly form crystalline structures of\nsilicon dioxide as obstacles wherever they want. In\naddition to being relatively easy to learn, it has a\nwide range of applications.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory023_m01_003: Stone of Lament\nThe caster can quickly synthesize and crystallize\nsilicon carbide in the air and fire the resulting stone\nat a target. The stones this magic creates have an\naerodynamic shape that makes them astoundingly\naccurate in finding their targets.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory023_m01_004: Glass Wheel\nThe caster forms shards of zirconium dioxide above\ntheir head and fires them at high speed at the target.\nIt is referred to as a wheel because of the\ncharacteristic circular trajectory drawn in the air\nwhile forming the crystals.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory024_t: Battle of Fezzan
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory024_m01_001: After the terrible Great Undoing that ravaged the\nsurface, Nuwa performed a crash landing in the\ndesert. They established a civilization, and 2,250\nyears afterward came an incident that would\ndetermine the future of Nuwa: the military conflict\nknown in the Dagdan Empire as the Battle of Fezzan.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory024_m01_002: Nuwa was discovered by the Dagdan Empire and\nattacked fiercely by three hundred thousand of their\ntroops. The increase in greenery in the desert due to\nclimate change was responsible for the weakening of\nthe artificial sandstorm that had provided cover for\nKunlun, resulting in our capture by the empire.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory024_m01_003: The imperial army was initially unable to crack the\nsturdy outer shell of Nuwa's residential sector. That\ndeadlock was broken when a single huge dragon\narrived and used its terrible power to destroy the\nouter shell. The situation changed for the worse\nwhen the imperial army flooded into the interior.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory024_m01_004: The dragon and our numbers disadvantage spelled\ncertain defeat. Our last resort was to employ Artemis,\nbut doing so on the dragon soaring above us would\nbe akin to calling down the wrath of the gods on\nourselves. I did not have the courage to give\nthe order.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory024_m01_005: Amidst the chaos of the battle, I received a\ndisturbing report that Sicyon, who had disappeared\nfrom Nuwa about five hundred years before, was\nseen among the enemies. I find it utterly impossible\nto believe that a Mediator might betray us. And yet...
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory024_m01_006: Many crew members were lost during the battle,\nincluding combat captain Roxana. When the hellish\nchaos subsided, we finally made the choice to\nsurrender. Many of our companions on the surface\nof the residential sector were taken away. Only the\nfew sheltering in the depths survived.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory024_m01_007: In this harsh desert, with most of Nuwa's life support\nsystems destroyed, it is uncertain how long the\nsurvivors may last. However, it is my duty as captain\nof Nuwa to see that they have a future.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory025_t: Great Undoing I
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory025_m01_001: It is tempting to say the tragedy started when a part\nof that thing was discovered in the strata exposed by\nthe collapse in the District 9 mountains. (Which itself\nwas caused by a massive earthquake that shook the\nentire continent.) But in fact, it all began much\nearlier than that.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory025_m01_002: The analysis of the tissue samples retrieved from\nthat thing were shocking. They were a near perfect\nmatch for records recovered from the mysterious\nhostile force believed to have fought with Craft 3,\nJörmungandr, before her disappearance 40 years ago.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory025_m01_003: All our assumptions had to be abandoned.\nJörmungandr was supposed to be sailing toward\ndistant Sirius A when she encountered the hostile\nforce, and her last known coordinates were 7.7\nlight-years away. How could anything identical to\nwhat destroyed her be found here?
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory025_m01_004: In the midst of the chaos, before I or any of the\nGrand Megaliths could form a working hypothesis,\nVritra gave the order to deploy Artemis's Arrow\nagainst the thing. But that just raised the question:\ndid Vritra know of our enemy's existence before\nwe did?
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory026_t: Great Undoing II
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory026_m01_001: At first, no one knew what that thing was. Was it a\nstructure or a creature? Organic or inorganic? Why\nwas it there, and how long ago did it arrive? We had\nno answers. As the samples were analyzed, it became\nclear that they came from a life-form composed\nmostly of silicon.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory026_m01_002: Based on those results, Vritra's decision to attack the\nthing with a superheavy metal round from Artemis\nwas a catastrophic error. The volley failed to destroy\nthe target, and only succeeded in fully awakening it.\nWhen we beheld the entirety of its stirring form,\nwe were seized with despair.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory026_m01_003: The thing was too massive to be considered a\ncreature—more like a living nightmare. It was far\nbigger than any building, mountain, or even the\nOuroboros-class generation ships. And it saw us,\nwho awakened it with our attack, as its foes.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory026_m01_004: But that was only the start. Huge creatures emerged\nfrom ancient ruins around the world and took flight.\nTheir forms resembled the dragons of myth. They\ngathered in one place as if called by that thing and\nbegan their counterattack.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory026_m01_005: Vritra gave the order to strike at them, and so we\nbarraged them with all our weapons. Yet they were\nunstoppable. We faced a world that was a month\naway from being scorched to cinders, with all trace\nof everything humanity had built being lost.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory026_m01_006: As I write this report in a corner of EX-017, the\nsubsurface zone where I shelter with my colleagues,\nI cannot help but ask how it came to this. What was\nthat thing? Where did it come from? And why was\nVritra so decisive in attacking it?
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory027_t: Odd Transmission
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory027_m01: <TH>
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory027_m01_001: If you are listening to this, I hope your journey has\nbeen safe thus far.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory027_m01_002: My name is Orpheus. I have been waiting for you for\na long time, Anatolia.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory027_m01_003: Anatolia, daughter of Nuwa. I will continue to wait\nfor you.
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory027_m01_004: Waiting for...when you come...to Solomon...
MID_LIB_Hub_Memory027_m01_Footer: <TEDF>